INSERT INTO feature VALUES('glf-face-theory','descriptions','GLF: the finite shape theory','glf-two-views','implemented','uncommon','dependent provers','Finite shapes as a FaceTT shape parameter with no interval: decidable subshapes with complements, meets, unions and the outer pushout (UnionSquare::mediator); atomic and conjunctive entailment (decide) with a Derivation or a Countermodel, each validated independently of the search; a conclusion''s column disjunctions admitted, as membership in a union, a disjunction across variables or in a premise refused at admission; evidence by meets, not case trees.','theory-shapes','crates/theory-shapes/tests/finite.rs crates/theory-shapes/tests/faces.rs','crate-tests','#640','#709 #885');
INSERT INTO feature VALUES('glf-lc-syntax-model','descriptions','The λ-calculus syntax model with its six substitution laws','glf-model-in-source','implemented','uncommon','dependent provers','The pure λ-calculus''s single-substitution calculus as `theory LC` (Con, Sub, Tm; nine operations; the six substitution laws) and its syntax model `module LCSyntax : Model(LC)` over de Bruijn terms, renamings and substitutions: laws 1, 2, 5 and 6 by computation, 3 and 4 by induction on the term through four fusion lemmas; every law a `Path` field discharged by `become` of a top-level lemma; the module packed into the record of LC''s models and a β-step run through it; 94 declarations, kernel-sealed. Lifting is a constructor (a definition refuses by #761, the pathological twin); `theory LC` is hand-written as `Lambda`''s first-order translation (#765); the theory''s own declaration refuses `OutOfFragment` (#522) while `Model(LC)` derives from its presentation.','surface-corpus','corpus/model/desc/lc/ corpus/model/desc/lc/lift-as-definition.gandr','corpus/model/desc/lc/lift-as-definition.gandr','#640','#788');
INSERT INTO feature VALUES('glf-model-in-source','theory','A model of a signature written in source; the shape parameter','glf-two-views','partial','unique','dependent provers','A first-order model of a signature is written as a record type in source — Model(Nat) as #{nat : Type, zero : () => nat, succ : (n : nat) => nat}, its syntax model inhabiting it, the module packed into it — and a theory block states the finite shape its cells are over (shape Square : 4 { left = {0, 2}; … }), a face refused outside the shape or repeated; the λ-calculus single-substitution model as a record waits on gandr #721, its syntax model (two laws by induction on a neutral) the next unit.','theory-levitation','corpus/model/desc/model-in-source.gandr','corpus/model/desc/model-in-source.gandr','#640','#734');
INSERT INTO feature VALUES('glf-two-views','descriptions','GLF: the two views of a signature','levitated-descriptions','implemented','uncommon','dependent provers','The first-order model generated from a signature code by the single-substitution fold; one generic evaluation and readback for every simply-sorted signature, identified with the first-order view on three signatures; the identity-return model''s judgements admitted by the kernel.','theory-levitation','crates/theory-levitation/tests/glf.rs','crate-tests','#640','#704');
INSERT INTO feature VALUES('grades','effects','Grades on a hold','temporary-access','partial','uncommon','mainstream languages','A hold written hold[1] s = e holds its value at grade one: the entry is a value made in place, the held value is never copied while held (a copying read refused by name), and exclusive accesses lend it; a string held at grade one is written in place, a copy refused by name. The bracket is a numeral; the default grade is unwritten. The emitter does not yet read the grade to drop the holder count on a write-back.','core-term core-checker surface-grammar surface-lowering','corpus/model/control/held-unique.gandr corpus/pathological/control/held-unique.gandr corpus/model/strings/unique-write.gandr corpus/pathological/strings/unique-write.gandr','corpus/model/control/held-unique.gandr','#1219','#1212 #1618');
